  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Catalyzing private sector commitment to implement the Bonn Challenge &#x2013; a platform for success</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To achieve the goals of the Bonn Challenge, additional investment is required from the private sector. The project therefore helped companies integrate forest and landscape restoration (FLR) into supply chains relevant for forests while it also promoted the FLR approach. The project identified methods, costs and benefits for this integration, and the results were used to develop business models that illustrate the economic, social and ecological benefits that FLR has to offer. FLR was also analysed in terms of its significance for the obligations needing to be met by the public and private sectors for zero net deforestation (ZND). Companies will be supported in their FLR and ZND activities by a knowledge community focusing on FLR in supply chains, which the project has set up based on business models and other experience with key private sector actors. A guideline to inform company initiatives and policymakers has also been produced.</narrative>
  </description>
